# Icons: use with icons (withicons.com)

Copy this file into `.cursor/rules/` of an app that uses with icons. Full skill: https://withicons.com/skill/SKILL.md

- Packages: `@withicons/react`, `vue`, `svelte`, `angular`, `solid`, `web` (custom element `<with-icon>` + icon classes), `static` (SVG + sprites), `core` (resolve/search), `motion` (optional animations).
- Imports are PascalCase of the kebab-case name: `import { ArrowRight, Trash } from '@withicons/react'`. Other styles are subpaths: `@withicons/react/solid` (also `/duo`, `/gloss`, `/engrave`, `/blueprint`, `/sketch`, `/glass`, `/kawaii`, `/sticker`, `/pixel`, `/retro`).
- **Never invent an icon name.** Aliases (`bin`, `gear`, `house`) are not exports. Look the name up with the `withicons` MCP server (`search_icons`), `npx withicons search <words>`, or `https://withicons.com/api/search?q=<words>`.
- Style: `line` for UI chrome, `solid` for active/selected states, `duo` for friendly cards. Creative styles (`gloss`, `engrave`, `blueprint`, `sketch`) and the multi-colour palette styles (`glass` glassmorphism, `kawaii` cute, `sticker` Y2K, `pixel` 8-bit, `retro` 70s) are for illustrations, heroes and slides at 32px or larger only. Use one style per UI region. Palette colours are CSS variables (`--with-<style>-<role>`); the ink follows `color`.
- Animation is optional and separate: `@withicons/motion` (with a bundler import `@withicons/motion/motion.css` + `@withicons/motion/icons.css`; from a CDN link `dist/motion.css` + one `dist/icons/<name>.css` per animated icon, never the all-icons `icons.css`; wrap the icon in `<span class="wm wm-loop" data-wm="<name>">`, `wm-hover` inside a `.wm-trigger` button, `wm-swap` for icon-to-icon). Ask the MCP `animate_icon` tool or `npx withicons animate <name>` for exact code. Keep loops to one or two per screen.
- Props: `size` (24), `color` (currentColor, so prefer CSS `color`), `strokeWidth` (line/duo/blueprint/sketch/kawaii only), `absoluteStrokeWidth`, `title`.
- Accessibility: decorative icons need nothing (aria-hidden by default). Icon-only buttons get `aria-label` on the `<button>`. Standalone meaningful icons get `title` (components) or `label` (`<with-icon>`).
- Avoid the generic `<Icon name=...>` component unless names are dynamic, because it bundles every icon. Do not use `<img>` for icons that must follow text colour. Serve sprites from the same origin.
- HTML without a build: `<script type="module" src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@withicons/web@0.2.0/dist/cdn.js"></script>` (loads only the icons on the page), then `<with-icon name="home" variant="solid"></with-icon>`. Icon classes: `<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@withicons/classes@0.2.0/dist/with-loader.js" defer></script>`, then `<i class="with with-home"></i>`. Never `with-all.css` in production (every icon in every style, ~6 MB gzipped).
